# Docker sends everything not excluded here to the build. Unlike .gitignore, patterns are anchored
# to the context root and * doesn't cross /, so use **/ for "at any depth". Every line should match
# something that exists in this repo.

# Secrets, at any depth and in any variant (.env, .env.local, .env.prod, ...). The image doesn't
# need .env.example either: config comes only from real env vars.
**/.env*

# Full history, including any secret ever committed and later deleted. It also changes on every
# commit, which would invalidate the COPY layer.
.git

# Local environment, caches and build output. The image builds its own .venv; a Windows one copied
# in would be useless (Scripts/, .exe files, Windows paths).
.venv
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[oc]
.ruff_cache
dist

# Docker's own files and dev-only tool config: not needed in the image, and leaving them out means
# editing them doesn't invalidate the COPY layer (and force a full reinstall).
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
.editorconfig
.gitattributes
.gitignore
.pre-commit-config.yaml
ruff.toml

# Docs and agent/CI config.
.github
.agents
.claude
docs
CLAUDE.md
